# Project Rules

`AGENTS.md` is the single source of truth for working in this repo. Read it first, then `DOCUMENTATION.md` (how it works) and `DESIGN.md` (how it looks). Do not duplicate their rules here.

## Stack (do not substitute)
- Astro 7 static site + React 19 islands, TypeScript strict, plain CSS, Supabase, Vercel.
- No Tailwind, no shadcn/ui, no Vite app shell, no server compute.

## UI work
- Read `DESIGN.md` before any UI change. Tokens live in `src/styles/theme.css`; `dashboard.css` and `loginModal.css` are layout only.
- Never hardcode colors, font sizes, spacing or shadows. Use the tokens.
- Reuse the existing primitives (`Button`, `Modal`, `CollapsibleCard`, `ConfirmModal`, `EmptyState`) before writing new ones.
- Mobile first, 44px minimum tap targets, every screen needs empty, loading and error states.
- User-facing copy is Spanish.

## Verification
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build`; the build must stay static (no `.vercel/output/functions/`).
- Verify UI from the source. Do not start a browser, Playwright or screenshots.

## Process
- Keep `DOCUMENTATION.md` current in the same change.
- Follow the prompt chain in `prompts/` for planned work.
- Do not add dependencies or change deploy shape without asking.
